{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-fix-expr-sql/findfirst-fresh-recordset",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-EXPR-1",
    "Branch D"
  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-expr-1/d-predicate-consumers: one recordset reused after the first NoMatch. Asks the FindFirst consumer of Null, 0, 1, -1, 2, 2.5, '', '1', '0', 'q', 'True' and CVErr(5), each on its own freshly opened dynaset of SELECT ID FROM One, with Errors read right after FindFirst and NoMatch after; the valid criteria ID = 1 (first and last) and ID = 2 are controls. Fixture r-fix-expr-sql-expr is opened read-only through DAO.DBEngine.120; each recordset reads Name, Type and Value of every field. Each statement is preceded by a marker (a DROP TABLE of a table that does not exist, which always fails), so DBEngine.Errors read after the statement shows that statement's own failure or the marker's, never an older one. Where Field Precision and Scale are read, the recordset is first positioned on its first row (MoveFirst) and DecimalPlaces is not read.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
  "pathBinding": "attempt-local-copy",
